module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_variant_construction_arm_body_not_typed

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }

data generic_variant_construction_arm_body_not_typed: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_variant_construction_arm_body_not_typed" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "For a match arm constructing a generic coproduct at its declared expected instantiation, infer derives the result and judges the payload through declared_type_inhabitance; a wrong payload refuses. Full instantiated-type controls and the wrong-instantiation control exercise this source route." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "RE-READ 2026-11-20 on main b94646b1a6c: the inference implementation already derives Outcome<ParseTree> for both g_constructor and g_tokenize_parse. The two failing claims required the obsolete underived-body advisory; their mbp_type_name projection also reported mbp_type_not_named for an Instantiation, not absence of grounding. Stronger controls compare the complete derived type to p.Outcome<p.ParseTree> and require the advisory absent; all 21 match controls execute green on srv1 with the existing compiler. The additional source specimen passes ParseArtifact to Accepted.value at Outcome<ParseTree>; assembly succeeds and infer refuses with record_field_value_does_not_inhabit at a node within g. The control requires that located reason, not the accompanying infer_grounding_not_derived advisories. No infer implementation changed. Historical receipts below preserve the superseded claim names and assertions at their cited revisions. Live DeclarationRef evidence points to mbt_a_generic_constructor_match_has_its_expected_instantiation_holds and mbt_a_constructor_at_the_wrong_instantiation_refuses_holds.",
    "INVALID STATE: a match arm whose body rebuilds a generic coproduct value from a constructor (`Rejected { diagnostics: r }`, `Accepted { value: artifact.tree, diagnostics: d }` over Outcome<T>) is accepted with its body type underived, so the match itself is untyped. HARM: loud and counted, never fabricated -- each such body is reported infer_match_arm_body_type_underived at its own locus -- but a mismatch between the constructed value and the function's declared return is not judged. Observed at gunbc origin/main e394f8cf042 by execution: v2.test.claim.match_binder.match_binder_typing mbt_an_underived_arm_body_is_a_counted_frontier_holds and mbt_the_sevens_call_scrutinee_is_typed_and_its_constructor_bodies_are_counted_holds, over g_constructor and the native seven. Split out of the retired rung drop match_arm_binder_typing_lost_to_lexical_carrier, whose population this row was never part of: the binder beneath these bodies is typed.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; the constructed type is decidable from the variant's declared payload instantiated by the expected type. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: infer derives a variant construction's type at a generic coproduct's instantiation taken from the expected position (the match's declared return), SUFFICIENT FOR the two rows above to flip to the arm bodies derived and a body constructed at the wrong instantiation to refuse. CAN CLIMB AFTER ONE GROUNDING: the expected-position instantiation is not yet threaded to infer_variant_construct_facts for a match arm body.",
    "SIGHTING (gunbc#16331, 2026-11-11): the two named rows -- `mbt_the_sevens_call_scrutinee_is_typed_and_its_constructor_bodies_are_counted_holds` and `mbt_an_underived_arm_body_is_a_counted_frontier_holds` in `src/v2/test/claim/match_binder/match_binder_typing.dag` -- PASSED at f08a6ae4 (the gunbc#15175 PARENT, measured `match_binder_typing` 20/20 by an offline `claim_batch`) and FAIL at 1056ea65. So they regressed somewhere after #15175 and BEHIND THE #15175 RESOLVE REFUSAL: from #15175 until gunbc#16331 the whole file was resolve-refused by the LocusAnchor member-equality wall (`d.head.at == node_locus(...)` on `v2.std.diagnostic::Locus` embedding `LocusAnchor<NodeOccurrence>`), so 0 of its 20 rows ran and this regression was invisible. gunbc#16331 (routing `Locus` to its `locus_eq` in `equality_route_declarations`) cleared the refusal and the file resolves; these two rows are then seen red while the other 18 pass. NOT caused by gunbc#16331: the regenerated `v1_compiler_infer.rs` mirror diff is confined to `equality_route_declarations()`, which neither row reads -- this is the same class the row already records (a constructor-body arm left on the counted frontier), surfacing again in the match-binder typing subsystem after #15175. No bisect performed.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_variant_construct_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.match_binder.match_binder_typing", decl_name: "mbt_a_constructor_at_the_wrong_instantiation_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.match_binder.match_binder_typing", decl_name: "mbt_a_generic_constructor_match_has_its_expected_instantiation_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
